{"slug":"suzanne-bonamici","qid":"Q45946","name":"Suzanne Bonamici","desc":"American politician","article":"Suzanne Bonamici","born":"1954-10-14","died":null,"birthplace":"Detroit","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"OR-01","f":2012,"u":null},{"t":"State Senate of Oregon","w":"","f":2008,"u":2011},{"t":"Oregon House of Representatives","w":"","f":2007,"u":2008}],"summary":"Suzanne Marie Bonamici ( BONN-ə-MEE-chee; born October 14, 1954) is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Oregon's 1st congressional district, a seat she was first elected to in a 2012 special election. The district includes most of Portland west of the Willamette River,  along with most of Portland's western suburbs such as Beaverton, Hillsboro, Tigard, and Lake Oswego.\nA Democrat, Bonamici represented the 17th district in the Oregon State Senate from 2008 to 2011.","photo":{"f":"suzanne-bonamici.jpg","by":"U.S. Congress","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suzanne_Bonamici.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","n":"Suzanne Bonamici","race":"OR-01"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":241556,"s":68.63,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":210682,"s":67.91,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":297071,"s":64.59,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":231198,"s":63.65,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":225391,"s":59.61,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":160038,"s":57.31,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"OR-01","p":"D","v":197845,"s":59.6,"w":true,"n":"Suzanne Bonamici"}]}